<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand coutumier de Normandie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand coutumier de Normandie is a compilation of the customary law of Normandy, written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> in the mid-thirteenth century and soon translated into French. Officially revised in 1583 as the Coutume de Normandie, it remained the law of the province until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. It still underlies the customary law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/channel-islands">Channel Islands</a> of Jersey and Guernsey.</p></div>
